  "drc_notes": {
    "_": "Adaptations vs the real sky130 deck. The engine has no derived layers in this load path, and min_enclosure/asymmetric_enclosure flag every inner shape not hosted by the outer layer, so enclosure rules whose inner layer legitimately appears outside the outer layer are inexpressible without false positives.",
    "licon.5_licon.8": "licon enclosure by diff (40) is expressed as min_extension diff-past-licon (LICON.5, one axis, overlapping pairs only) because one licon layer serves both diff and poly contacts. licon enclosure by poly (50/80) is omitted: generators draw poly as multiple overlapping rects and the per-polygon extension check would false-positive on every gate-stub contact.",
    "nwell.enclosure": "nwell enclosure of p+ diff (180) omitted: no derived pdiff layer; every NMOS diff would be flagged as unhosted. Construction-side cell.nwell_diff_enc=180 enforces it at generation time.",
    "nsdm_psdm.enclosure": "nsdm/psdm enclosure of diff (125) omitted for the same derived-layer reason; implants are emitted as cell bboxes by the flow.",
    "via.1_exact_size": "via1 cut is drawn at VIA.1 min_width (150) by the per-layer via sizing; max_width omitted since 150 is already the exact size.",
    "VIA2.1_relaxed": "real via2 minimum size is 200; min_width 170 kept from the widen pass \u2014 the per-layer flow draws via2 at 170, VIA2.1.EXACT keeps the real 200 upper bound.",
    "ENC.VIA.4A_key": "Historical: these keys were named to sort (BTreeMap) ahead of the generic mcon min_enclosure because the flow once sized met2 landing pads from the FIRST min_enclosure rule of any layer pair. The flow now does a (outer,inner)-filtered lookup, so key naming is free; keys kept for stability.",
    "routing_stack": "cell.layers.routing_metals spans the full met1-met5 stack. The flow derives per-layer wire widths, via cut sizes, and landing-pad dims from these DRC rules (max of layer min width, ERC EM width, cut+enclosures, min-area square), and thins upper-layer track density so wide layers (met4 via4 pads, met5 1600nm wires) stay spacing-legal on the uniform track grid.",
    "erc.p2p": "p2p_r_limit_ohm=500 is the analog block-level calibration: normal bias nets measure 50-110 ohm and must not flag; only genuinely resistive nets (kilo-ohm unstrapped poly/thin rails) should trip it."
  },
